// Copy to Signing.local.xcconfig — that name is gitignored — and fill both in.
// Signing.xcconfig includes it last, so these two win over the defaults.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM — your Apple team id. Xcode → Settings → Accounts → your
// account → the Team ID column. Or read it off a profile you already have:
//
//   security cms -D -i ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/UserData/Provisioning\ Profiles/<uuid>.mobileprovision \
//     | plutil -extract Entitlements.application-identifier raw -
//
// which prints TEAMID.bundle.id — both halves of what this file needs.
//
// PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER — must be a bundle id your team has a profile for.
// A free personal team will issue one on demand for any id nobody else has
// claimed, so make it yours: dev.comet.native.<yourname>. Do NOT leave this
// line out; the default dev.cometnative.Comet belongs to no personal team, and
// the failure reads as "No profiles for 'dev.cometnative.Comet' were found",
// which does not sound like a bundle-id problem.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = dev.comet.native.yourname
